hen youâ€™re responsibilities-maxxing, sometimes you need the opposite. A blowout. A huge, transcendent, resetting release. A rave.</p><p>I donâ€™t know what took me so long to get around to it. Misplaced parental guilt? Internalised ageism? Exhaustion? Itâ€™s not as though I didnâ€™t know other gen-Xers who have been regularly getting blissfully â€“ ceremonially, even â€“ lost in house, techno or drumâ€™nâ€™bass, and theyâ€™re not alone. <a href="https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/10.1177/03057356251329229">A 2025 study</a> by the University of Leeds went viral: â€œ<a href="https://www.instagram.com/p/DXmbIDPDbpf/">Women aged 40-65 are turning to raves for real mental health</a>,â€ said one of many Instagram posts and press headlines. â€œ<a href="https://www.instagram.com/p/DZbTO7vFcNi/?img_index=1">Why many women over 40 still go to raves</a>,â€ read another. But surely the question should be: why the hell wouldnâ€™t they?</p> <a href="https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/2026/jul/20/the-rave-secret-why-middle-aged-women-are-larging-it-and-seeing-big-health-benefits">Continue reading...</a>ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;EDxky3k9xDV4-V2OQStF6DeZFXW7ebt1XLioC_fXre4ƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkx9ni:///sha-256;3c1UmEIJrC4bta04n2dCHe14hpkR2x_TAXiKwot0Rbkƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;SnhVwW0xmn4Hlj7KTh9H2s6GL7VswRcFxxvzGxpm6ggƒdpairƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;2hB-8fUsxQ-e9Zq86lsI8J4OxETAC0larHnVjNcR-zoƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarkefalseƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;FUQ5SMo48_WIqCbIhVIkrvhgIN_wLrmXI5z54Yofa6Qƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarkdtrueƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;EzBdVw8eOCU