times you need the opposite. A blowout. A huge, transcendent, resetting release. A rave.</p><p>I donâ€™t know what took me so long to get around to it. Misplaced parental guilt? Internalised ageism? Exhaustion? Itâ€™s not as though I didnâ€™t know other gen-Xers who have been regularly getting blissfully â€“ ceremonially, even â€“ lost in house, techno or drumâ€™nâ€™bass, and theyâ€™re not alone. <a href="https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/10.1177/03057356251329229">A 2025 study</a> by the University of Leeds went viral: â€œ<a href="https://www.instagram.com/p/DXmbIDPDbpf/">Women aged 40-65 are turning to raves for real mental health</a>,â€ said one of many Instagram posts and press headlines. â€œ<a href="https://www.instagram.com/p/DZbTO7vFcNi/?img_index=1">Why many women over 40 still go to raves</a>,â€ read another. But surely the question should be: why the hell wouldnâ€™t they?</p> <a href="https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/2026/jul/20/the-rave-secret-why-middle-aged-women-are-larging-it-and-seeing-big-health-benefits">Continue reading...</a>ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;oR1u-9gWVxvsVc4bvqdUb27k2f5LXy5_iPJUh6C8fCkƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkxXThe rave secret: why middle-aged women are larging it â€“ and seeing big health benefitsƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;7EdXjwhDSFGtWyKBQuMXUVSeDVwEHpXIKxhFaclXwbcƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkoSyndicationItemƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;I2pO2o6m328P2jipxM1IYh1KZh0Mi-MIdkhTZ3Ad7Swƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkxˆhttps://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/2026/jul/20/the-rave-secret-why-middle-aged-women-are-larging-it-and-seeing-big-health-benefitsƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;j5f5P7rzM9Gost497DDCeG2vk38xV48rylD_nCTQb3sƒdpairƒeri